function throttle(fn, ms) {
  let last = 0;
  return (...args) => {
    const now = Date.now();
    if (now - last >= ms) {
      last = now;
      fn(...args);
    }
  };
}

window.addEventListener('scroll', throttle(onScroll, 200), { passive: true });
```

Leading-edge: fires on the first event, then ignores calls until 200 ms have passed.

Gotcha: no trailing call → the last scroll position can be missed if scrolling stops inside the window. If the final position matters, add a `scrollend` listener or use lodash `throttle` (trailing by default) if already installed.

